<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Ping–pong on ratios and exponential growth</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove the case where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> is an integer in Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 1.2. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, we will follow a similar strategy to the negative evaluation case. We choose an initial graph <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}=K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}=K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and show that operations <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the concatenation of two consecutive <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> operations, act on attainable vector ratios with disjoint images. A simple calculation then shows that there exist exponentially many <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>–attainable vectors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that for <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\binom{x}{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\binom{x}{y}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have defined <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(v)\coloneqq x/y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(v)\coloneqq x/y</annotation></semantics></math>. The following definition is a direct analogy of Definition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem9" title="Definition 2.9. ‣ 2.5. Ping–pong on ratios and exponential growth ‣ 2. Negative evaluations and chromatic reciprocity ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a word in the semigroup <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B,D\}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B,D\}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a planar graph, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> be an edge of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}(a,G,e)\coloneqq(w\circ a_{t}\circ a_{t-1}\circ\dots\circ a_{1})(G,e)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}(a,G,e)\coloneqq(w\circ a_{t}\circ a_{t-1}\circ\dots\circ a_{1})(G,e),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">the attainable vector witnessed by the pair generated through the sequence of operations encoded by <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> starting with the pair <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,e)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove a lemma analogous to Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem10" title="Lemma 2.10. ‣ 2.5. Ping–pong on ratios and exponential growth ‣ 2. Negative evaluations and chromatic reciprocity ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}\coloneqq w(K_{3},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}\coloneqq w(K_{3},e)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is one of the edges of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{0}=\binom{q(q-1)}{q(q-1)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{0}=\binom{q(q-1)}{q(q-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w_{0})=1/(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w_{0})=1/(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, on ratios, the operations <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> act by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B}(r)=\frac{(q-1)r}{r+q-2},\qquad f_{D}(r)=\frac{r+q-2}{(q-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B}(r)=\frac{(q-1)r}{r+q-2},\qquad f_{D}(r)=\frac{r+q-2}{(q-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\coloneqq(1/q,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\coloneqq(1/q,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B}(I)\subseteq\bigl(1/(q-1),\,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B}(I)\subseteq\bigl(1/(q-1),\,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}(I)\subseteq\bigl(1/q,\,1/(q-1)\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}(I)\subseteq\bigl(1/q,\,1/(q-1)\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the images are disjoint and contained in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\neq w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\neq w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are words in the semigroup <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B,D\}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B,D\}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))\neq r(\mathbf{w}(w^{\prime},K_{3},e))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))\neq r(\mathbf{w}(w^{\prime},K_{3},e))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The base computation is immediate: <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{3}/e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{3}/e</annotation></semantics></math> is a double edge, so <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{K_{3}/e}(q)=q(q-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{K_{3}/e}(q)=q(q-1)</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{3}-e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{3}-e</annotation></semantics></math> is the path on three vertices, so <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{K_{3}-e}(q)=q(q-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{K_{3}-e}(q)=q(q-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w_{0})\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w_{0})\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3 (Matrix action). ‣ 4.1. Attainable vectors ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, if <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\binom{x}{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\binom{x}{y}</annotation></semantics></math> then</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Bw=\binom{(q-1)x}{x+(q-2)y},\qquad Dw=\binom{x+(q-2)y}{(q-1)^{2}y}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Bw=\binom{(q-1)x}{x+(q-2)y},\qquad Dw=\binom{x+(q-2)y}{(q-1)^{2}y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">so the ratio maps are <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B},f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B},f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now fix <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/q&lt;r&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/q&lt;r&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, since <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing, so</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B}(r)&gt;f_{B}(1/q)=\frac{1}{q-1}\quad\text{and}\quad f_{B}(r)&lt;f_{B}(1)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B}(r)&gt;f_{B}(1/q)=\frac{1}{q-1}\quad\text{and}\quad f_{B}(r)&lt;f_{B}(1)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{B}(I)\subseteq(1/(q-1),\,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{B}(I)\subseteq(1/(q-1),\,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, since <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly increasing,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}(r)&gt;f_{D}(1/q)=\frac{1}{q}\quad\text{and}\quad f_{D}(r)&lt;f_{D}(1)=\frac{1}{q-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}(r)&gt;f_{D}(1/q)=\frac{1}{q}\quad\text{and}\quad f_{D}(r)&lt;f_{D}(1)=\frac{1}{q-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{D}(I)\subseteq(1/q,\,1/(q-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{D}(I)\subseteq(1/q,\,1/(q-1))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the images are disjoint.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, suppose <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))=r(\mathbf{w}(w^{\prime},K_{3},e))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))=r(\mathbf{w}(w^{\prime},K_{3},e))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then their ratios agree and lie in <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>. If at least one of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w,w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is empty, say <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))=r(w(K_{3},e))=1/(q-1)\not\in f_{B}(I)\cup f_{D}(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e))=r(w(K_{3},e))=1/(q-1)\not\in f_{B}(I)\cup f_{D}(I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> must also be empty.
If both <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w,w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-empty, by the image disjointness just proved, the last letter of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> must equal the last letter of <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since both matrices in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3 (Matrix action). ‣ 4.1. Attainable vectors ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> are invertible, we can cancel the last letter and iterate to conclude <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to prove Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the set <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> of words <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\left\{B,D\right\}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\left\{B,D\right\}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b+2d=n-3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b+2d=n-3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of letters <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of letters <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that a simple recursive argument shows that <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W|=F_{n-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W|=F_{n-2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(F_{n})_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(F_{n})_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Fibonacci sequence.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, notice that every word <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W</annotation></semantics></math> yields an <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>–vertex witness and an <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>–attainable vector <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}(w,K_{3},e)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 4.5. ‣ 4.2. Ping–pong on ratios and exponential growth ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>, these <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{n-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{n-2}</annotation></semantics></math> vectors are all distinct. Applying Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (Square-root lemma). ‣ 4.1. Attainable vectors ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> finishes the proof:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathsf{S}^{\pl}_{n}(q)|\geq\sqrt{F_{n-2}}=\Theta(\varphi^{n/2}).\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>pl</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathsf{S}^{\pl}_{n}(q)|\geq\sqrt{F_{n-2}}=\Theta(\varphi^{n/2}).\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>A planar ping–pong for <math id="S5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we show that, for every fixed <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can obtain exponentially many distinct values of <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> already by ranging over simple, planar graphs <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, thus completing the proof of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1.1. ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.
Unlike the clique–join reduction (Section <a href="#S3" title="3. Non-integer positive evaluations via clique joins ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the argument here preserves planarity: it only uses the local planar operations <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> from Section <a href="#S2" title="2. Negative evaluations and chromatic reciprocity ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We show the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathsf{S}^{\mathrm{pl}}_{n}(q)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>pl</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathsf{S}^{\mathrm{pl}}_{n}(q)|</annotation></semantics></math> grows exponentially in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathsf{S}^{\mathrm{pl}}_{n}(q)|\;=\;2^{\Omega_{q}(n)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>pl</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn> 2</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathsf{S}^{\mathrm{pl}}_{n}(q)|\;=\;2^{\Omega_{q}(n)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Section <a href="#S1" title="1. Introduction ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we postpone the quantitative bounds until Remark <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Remark 5.4 (The dependence on 𝑞 or lack thereof). ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>. Similar to Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> follows a ping–pong/free-semigroup argument on the ratio of attainable vectors (see Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1. Attainable vectors ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> for the definition), but using <em id="S5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">higher powers</em> of <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and concatenations of <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the following lemma, which gives the ratio action of a block operation of higher powers of <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r\circ w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)=\frac{1}{q}+\frac{(r\circ w)(G,e)-\frac{1}{q}}{(q-1)^{2m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r\circ w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)=\frac{1}{q}+\frac{(r\circ w)(G,e)-\frac{1}{q}}{(q-1)^{2m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the computation in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 4.5. ‣ 4.2. Ping–pong on ratios and exponential growth ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> we see that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r\circ S^{2})(u)=\frac{r(u)+q-2}{(q-1)^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r\circ S^{2})(u)=\frac{r(u)+q-2}{(q-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for every attainable vector <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, when <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(w\circ S^{2i})(G,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(w\circ S^{2i})(G,e)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1,\dots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1,\dots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q-1)^{2i+2}(r\circ w\circ S^{2i+2})(G,e)=(q-1)^{2i}(r\circ w\circ S^{2i})(G,e)+(q-1)^{2i}(q-2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q-1)^{2i+2}(r\circ w\circ S^{2i+2})(G,e)=(q-1)^{2i}(r\circ w\circ S^{2i})(G,e)+(q-1)^{2i}(q-2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">These equations telescope into</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q-1)^{2m}(r\circ w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)=(r\circ w)(G,e)+(q-2)\frac{(q-1)^{2m}-1}{(q-1)^{2}-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q-1)^{2m}(r\circ w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)=(r\circ w)(G,e)+(q-2)\frac{(q-1)^{2m}-1}{(q-1)^{2}-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies (<a href="#S5.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Using these block operations of higher powers of <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we can prove the following ping–pong lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exists a planar graph <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, an edge <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and block operations <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=K(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=K(q)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=L(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=L(q)</annotation></semantics></math> that are each a sequence of operations in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B,S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B,S\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following is true. If, for every word <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in the semigroup <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{K,L\}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{K,L\}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(a)\coloneqq(w\circ a_{t}\circ a_{t-1}\circ\dots\circ a_{1})(G_{0},e_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(a)\coloneqq(w\circ a_{t}\circ a_{t-1}\circ\dots\circ a_{1})(G_{0},e_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the attainable vector witnessed by the pair generated through the sequence of operations encoded by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> starting with the pair <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{0},e_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{0},e_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, then for all words <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\neq w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\neq w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in the semigroup <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{K,L\}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{K,L\}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> with the same number of letters, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w)\neq\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w)\neq\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by remarking that in order to prove that a tuple <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G_{0},e_{0},K,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G_{0},e_{0},K,L)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the desired property, it is sufficient to find disjoint sets <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w(G_{0},e_{0}))\in I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w(G_{0},e_{0}))\in I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r((w\circ K)(G,e))\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r((w\circ K)(G,e))\in I</annotation></semantics></math>, for every edge <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> of a planar graph <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w(G,e))\in I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w(G,e))\in I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r((w\circ L)(G,e))\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r((w\circ L)(G,e))\in J</annotation></semantics></math>, for every edge <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> of a planar graph <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w(G,e))\in I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w(G,e))\in I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, let <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w,w^{\prime}\in\left\{K,L\right\}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w,w^{\prime}\in\left\{K,L\right\}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w)=\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w)=\widetilde{\mathbf{w}}(w^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w)=(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w)=(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S5.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we directly get <math id="S5.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, from (<a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="Item 1 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)–(<a href="#S5.I1.i3" title="Item 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) it follows that <math id="S5.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w^{\prime\prime})\in I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r\circ\widetilde{\mathbf{w}})(w^{\prime\prime})\in I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math> for any prefix <math id="S5.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S5.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, as <math id="S5.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint, <math id="S5.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> must agree in their last letter by (<a href="#S5.I1.i2" title="Item 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.I1.i3" title="Item 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). As <math id="S5.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\not\in\left\{0,1,2\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\not\in\left\{0,1,2\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to invertible matrices, hence the same is true for <math id="S5.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we may invert to cancel the action of the last letter and iterate to conclude that <math id="S5.p6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We divide the proof into three cases, depending on <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Case 1:</em><span id="S5.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> <math id="S5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,3/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,3/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X=(G_{0},e_{0},K,L,I,J)=\Big(K_{4},e,S^{2m},B^{2},\big(-\infty,(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3)\big],\big((q-1)^{2}/(2q-3),0\big)\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(G_{0},e_{0},K,L,I,J)=\Big(K_{4},e,S^{2m},B^{2},\big(-\infty,(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3)\big],\big((q-1)^{2}/(2q-3),0\big)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is any edge of <math id="S5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}=K_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}=K_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=m(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=m(q)</annotation></semantics></math> is an integer to be chosen later.
We now prove that <math id="S5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies properties (<a href="#S5.I1.i1" title="Item 1 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)–(<a href="#S5.I1.i3" title="Item 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w(G_{0},e_{0}))=1/(q-2)\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w(G_{0},e_{0}))=1/(q-2)\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 5.2. ‣ 5. A planar ping–pong for 𝑞∈(0,2)∖{1} ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, if <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r(w(G,e))\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r(w(G,e))\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}=(w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}=(w\circ S^{2m})(G,e)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w_{k})=\frac{r}{(q-1)^{2m}}+\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{(q-1)^{2m}}\right)&lt;\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{(q-1)^{2m}}\right)\overset{m\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}-\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w_{k})=\frac{r}{(q-1)^{2m}}+\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{(q-1)^{2m}}\right)&lt;\frac{1}{q}\left(1-\frac{1}{(q-1)^{2m}}\right)\overset{m\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}-\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, for sufficiently large <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="S5.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w_{k})\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w_{k})\in I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 4.3 (Matrix action). ‣ 4.1. Attainable vectors ‣ 4. The planar evaluation spectrum for 𝑞&gt;2 ‣ Chromatic polynomial evaluation spectra" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(w\circ B^{2})(G,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(w\circ B^{2})(G,e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}(q-1)^{2}&amp;0\\
2q-3&amp;(q-2)^{2}\end{pmatrix}w(G,e)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}(q-1)^{2}&amp;0\\
2q-3&amp;(q-2)^{2}\end{pmatrix}w(G,e).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r(w(G,e))\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r(w(G,e))\in(-\infty,0)=I\cup J</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell}=(w\circ B^{2})(G,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell}=(w\circ B^{2})(G,e)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(q-1)^{2}}{2q-3}&lt;r(w_{\ell})=\frac{(q-1)^{2}}{(2q-3)+(q-2)^{2}r^{-1}}&lt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(q-1)^{2}}{2q-3}&lt;r(w_{\ell})=\frac{(q-1)^{2}}{(2q-3)+(q-2)^{2}r^{-1}}&lt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I2.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">since <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2q-3&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2q-3&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S5.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(w_{\ell})\in J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(w_{\ell})\in J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Case 2:</em><span id="S5.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text"> <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(3/2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(3/2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(G_{0},e_{0},K,L,I,J)=\Big(K_{3},e,S^{2m},B^{2},\big[(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3),\infty\big),(1,(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3))\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(G_{0},e_{0},K,L,I,J)=\Big(K_{3},e,S^{2m},B^{2},\big[(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3),\infty\big),(1,(q-1)^{2}/(2q-3))\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
